stume Design"},{"source":"work_aw388","target":"work_aw392","type":"work_work","relation_type":"influenced","relation_note":"This film features a similar narrative of an unconventional teacher inspiring students to challenge societal norms and think critically within a rigid academic institution, directly echoing 'Dead Poets Society's' central premise."},{"source":"work_aw388","target":"work_aw393","type":"work_work","relation_type":"influenced","relation_note":"This film continues the tradition of showcasing a passionate teacher who uses unconventional methods and the power of literature to inspire and transform the lives of their students, much like John Keating."},{"source":"work_aw388","target":"work_aw389","type":"work_work","relation_type":"inspired_by","relation_note":"The film directly references Walt Whitman's poetry, particularly 'O Captain! My Captain!', to symbolize Keating's role as a mentor and the students' eventual defiance against conformity."},{"source":"work_aw388","target":"work_aw390","type":"work_work","relation_type":"inspired_by","relation_note":"This film established a precedent for the 'maverick teacher' archetype who challenges the educational establishment and inspires students, a core theme central to 'Dead Poets Society'."},{"source":"work_aw388","target":"work_aw391","type":"work_work","relation_type":"inspired_by","relation_note":"The film shares a similar New England boarding school setting and explores themes of intense male friendships, rebellion, and tragic coming-of-age within a rigid academic environment, echoing the student experience."}],"stats":{"total_nodes":21,"total_edges":20,"hop_0_count":1,"hop_1_count":20,"hop_2_count":0,"hop_3_count":0,"phantom_count":21,"vault_count":0}}